<%!-- Follow-only federation (Vutuv.Fediverse), the member's own page.

This page answers ONE question for someone who has never heard the word
"Fediverse": do I want this, yes or no. So it leads with what happens in plain
terms, then the switch, then — once the switch is on — the two things that make
it worth having: the handle to hand out, and the people who followed.

Account migration used to sit here too, in both directions, between the switch
and the Save button. It taxed every beginner with a raw actor-URI textarea they
would never use, and its two directions read as the same thing. It has its own
subpage now (/settings/fediverse/move), linked from the footer below. --%>
<.settings_shell user={@user} active={:fediverse} title={gettext("Fediverse")}>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <.card>
      <.section_title>{gettext("Followers from other networks")}</.section_title>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {gettext(
          "Beside vutuv there are thousands of independent social websites that all talk to each other. Mastodon is the best known of them. Together they are called the Fediverse."
        )}
      </p>

      <%!-- The "why would I want this" answer, which the old page never gave.
            Three short lines beat one dense paragraph for a decision. --%>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        {gettext("If you take part:")}
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-300">•</span>
          {gettext("People there can follow you without opening a vutuv account.")}
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-300">•</span>
          {gettext("Your public vutuv posts show up in their timelines.")}
        </li>
        <%!-- The inbound direction (issue #1160). It belongs in the sales pitch
              and not only in the card below, because the card is the thing you
              only reach once you have already said yes. --%>
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-300">•</span>
          {gettext("You can follow accounts there yourself, straight from vutuv.")}
        </li>
        <li class="flex gap-2">
          <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-300">•</span>
          {gettext("Nothing changes on vutuv itself, and you can switch it off again.")}
        </li>
      </ul>

      <.form
        :let={f}
        for={@changeset}
        action={~p"/settings/fediverse"}
        id="fediverse-form"
        class="mt-5 space-y-5"
      >
        <.form_error changeset={@changeset} />

        <%!-- Set to "1" by whichever consent modal the member agreed to. Empty
              on a plain submit, which sends them to the full-page confirmation
              instead (see fediverse_confirm.html.heex), so the switch cannot
              flip unacknowledged with or without JavaScript. --%>
        <input type="hidden" name="fediverse_ack" value="" data-fediverse-ack />

        <.setting_toggle label={gettext("Take part in the Fediverse")}>
          <:checkbox>
            <%= checkbox f, :fediverse_followers?, class: checkbox_class(), data: [fediverse_switch: true] %>
          </:checkbox>
          {gettext(
            "Off means your profile cannot be found there and nothing is sent. Posts already delivered may stay on those servers, beyond our reach."
          )}
        </.setting_toggle>

        <%!-- Reactions (issue #1068): the answer coming back. Only meaningful
              once posts are actually going out, so it shows with the rest of
              the "you are taking part" block. The wording names what is stored
              about a stranger, because that is the part a member is deciding
              about — and it has to stay true to the line under the post, which
              names those accounts rather than merely counting them. --%>
        <.setting_toggle
          :if={Vutuv.Fediverse.federated?(@user)}
          label={gettext("Show reactions from other networks")}
        >
          <:checkbox><%= checkbox f, :fediverse_reactions?, class: checkbox_class() %></:checkbox>
          {gettext(
            "Show under each of your posts who out there liked or shared it, by their account address on their own server, linked to that account. Visible to everyone who sees the post. We keep nothing else about these people: no name, no picture, no text. Switching it off deletes what is stored for it."
          )}
        </.setting_toggle>

        <%!-- Replies (issues #1069 and #1071): its own switch, off by default,
              because this is the one thing here that stores what somebody else
              wrote. The wording says the three things that decide it: you get
              to read the answers, we keep a copy for a while, and you can throw
              any of it away. --%>
        <.setting_toggle
          :if={Vutuv.Fediverse.federated?(@user)}
          label={gettext("Show replies from other networks")}
        >
          <:checkbox><%= checkbox f, :fediverse_replies?, class: checkbox_class() %></:checkbox>
          {gettext(
            "Answers people write out there appear under your post, marked as coming from another network. We keep a copy for up to six months and check now and then whether it is still published; if the author deletes it, ours goes too. You can remove any single reply, and switching this off deletes all of them."
          )}
        </.setting_toggle>

        <div class="pt-1">
          <.button type="submit">{gettext("Save")}</.button>
        </div>
      </.form>
    </.card>

    <%!-- Once the switch is on, the payoff: the handle to hand out (with the
          shared data-copy button, since copying it IS the action people come
          for) and the people who followed. Deliberately a card of its own —
          on the old page this was a grey readout box wedged above the form. --%>
    <.card :if={Vutuv.Fediverse.federated?(@user)}>
      <.section_title>{gettext("Your Fediverse handle")}</.section_title>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {gettext(
          "Give this out the way you give out an email address. Anyone on Mastodon and friends can paste it into their search and follow you from there."
        )}
      </p>
      <div class="mt-3 flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 px-3 py-2 ring-1 ring-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-800/50 dark:ring-slate-700">
        <code
          id="fediverse-handle"
          class="min-w-0 flex-1 select-all break-all text-sm text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-100"
        >{VutuvWeb.Fediverse.Docs.handle(@user)}</code>
        <button
          type="button"
          data-copy
          data-copy-target="fediverse-handle"
          data-label-copy={gettext("Copy")}
          data-label-copied={gettext("Copied")}
          class="shrink-0 rounded-md bg-white px-2 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 ring-1 ring-slate-200 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 dark:ring-slate-700 dark:hover:bg-slate-700"
        >
          {gettext("Copy")}
        </button>
      </div>

      <h3 class="mt-6 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        {ngettext(
          "%{formatted} follower from other networks",
          "%{formatted} followers from other networks",
          @follower_count,
          formatted: compact_count(@follower_count)
        )}
      </h3>

      <%!-- No preview list here: the followers live on their own page as a
            searchable, sortable, paginated table with the date each follow
            arrived. Repeating the newest few as bare lines said the same thing
            worse, so this card just points at it. --%>
      <%= if @follower_count == 0 do %>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          {gettext(
            "Nobody yet. Post your handle where people can see it, and the first follows will show up here."
          )}
        </p>
      <% else %>
        <.card_footer_link href={~p"/settings/fediverse/followers"} id="all-followers-link">
          {gettext("All followers")}
        </.card_footer_link>
      <% end %>
    </.card>

    <%!-- The other direction (issue #1160). Its own card rather than a second
          heading in the handle card: following somebody out there is a thing
          you go and do, not a readout of what happened to you, and burying the
          only way to start it under the follower count would hide it.

          Rendered for EVERY member, not only for one who already federates.
          Behind the switch it would be invisible to exactly the person the
          following page's own "here is why you cannot yet, here is the switch"
          panel was written for. --%>
    <.card>
      <.section_title>{gettext("Accounts you follow elsewhere")}</.section_title>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        {gettext(
          "It works the other way round too: paste somebody's address from Mastodon and friends, and you follow them from here."
        )}
      </p>

      <h3
        :if={Vutuv.Fediverse.federated?(@user) and @following_count > 0}
        class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white"
      >
        {ngettext(
          "You follow %{formatted} account on another network",
          "You follow %{formatted} accounts on other networks",
          @following_count,
          formatted: compact_count(@following_count)
        )}
      </h3>

      <.card_footer_link href={~p"/settings/fediverse/following"} id="all-following-link">
        <%= if @following_count == 0 do %>
          {gettext("Follow somebody out there")}
        <% else %>
          {gettext("Manage who you follow")}
        <% end %>
      </.card_footer_link>
    </.card>

    <%!-- The two neighbouring topics, as quiet links rather than full cards:
          the expert migration subpage (only while federating, where it can
          take effect) and the rel=me verification, which needs no federation
          at all and is one sentence. --%>
    <.card>
      <.section_title>{gettext("Related")}</.section_title>
      <div class="mt-2 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <p :if={Vutuv.Fediverse.federated?(@user)}>
          {gettext("Moving to or away from another Fediverse account?")}
          <.link
            navigate={~p"/settings/fediverse/move"}
            id="fediverse-move-link"
            class="font-semibold text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700 dark:text-brand-400 dark:hover:text-brand-300"
          >
            {gettext("Move your account")} ›
          </.link>
        </p>
        <%!-- The one thing a follow cannot do (issue #1211): it only ever brings
              what an account posts from now on, so the post somebody actually
              read out there is fetched by its address instead. --%>
        <p>
          {gettext("Read something out there that you want to answer from here?")}
          <.link
            navigate={~p"/system/fediverse/lookup"}
            id="fediverse-lookup-link"
            class="font-semibold text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700 dark:text-brand-400 dark:hover:text-brand-300"
          >
            {gettext("Look up a post by its address")} ›
          </.link>
        </p>
        <p>
          {gettext(
            "Want the checkmark on your Mastodon profile? That works without taking part here: your vutuv profile links your listed accounts with rel=\"me\"."
          )}
          <.link
            href={~p"/settings/social_media_accounts"}
            class="font-semibold text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700 dark:text-brand-400 dark:hover:text-brand-300"
          >
            {gettext("Manage social media accounts")} ›
          </.link>
        </p>
      </div>
    </.card>
  </div>

  <%!-- The two consent dialogs, one per direction of the switch. Hidden until
        the fediverseConsent enhancement in app.js opens the matching one on
        submit; its confirm button sets the ack field and submits for real. With
        JS off neither is ever seen and the plain submit lands on the
        full-page confirmation, which asks the same question with the same
        words. Same overlay recipe as the birthday-remove dialog. --%>
  <div
    :for={
      {id, on?} <- [{"fediverse-consent-on", true}, {"fediverse-consent-off", false}]
    }
    id={id}
    class="hidden fixed inset-0 z-[60] items-center justify-center p-4 [&:not(.hidden)]:flex"
    role="dialog"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-labelledby={"#{id}-title"}
    data-block-shortcuts
  >
    <div data-fediverse-consent-backdrop class="absolute inset-0 bg-slate-900/50 backdrop-blur-sm">
    </div>
    <div class="relative w-full max-w-lg rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-xl ring-1 ring-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:ring-slate-800">
      <.fediverse_consent_notice switching_on={on?} title_id={"#{id}-title"} />
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap justify-end gap-3">
        <button
          type="button"
          data-fediverse-consent-cancel
          class="rounded-lg bg-slate-100 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 dark:hover:bg-slate-700"
        >
          {gettext("Cancel")}
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          data-fediverse-consent-confirm
          class="rounded-lg bg-brand-600 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-brand-700"
        >
          <%= if on? do %>
            {gettext("I understand, take part")}
          <% else %>
            {gettext("I understand, switch off")}
          <% end %>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</.settings_shell>
